      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · the outline's five forms; A29 delegated labour",
          "title": "The plate and its five preparations",
          "italic": "Preparation embodies an affirmative office: another's labour can make an encounter possible — the question is whether it stays answerable to what was prepared.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The plate gives the question something determinate to meet: a document, an account, a testimony, an argument. Provenance matters from first contact — who produced the material, what it actually says, what work prepared it; the existence of a document and the truth of inferences from it are different matters. The outline gives preparation five forms: raw food carries the demanding texture of primary material; cooked food figures responsible interpretation making difficult material accessible through context; heavily processed food figures a product whose earlier transformations have become hard to recover; junk food figures the pursuit",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "of stimulation after the relation to nourishment has fallen away; fermentation figures inherited practices through which earlier participants have worked on what a newcomer receives. These are roles in an authored information ecology, not a dietary ranking. Cooking's affirmative office: a translation or careful explanation can open a route into the source — the question is whether that preparation remains answerable to what was prepared and leaves the recipient able to examine, disagree and continue. A29 follows what happens when the finished product is accepted but the conditions and costs of its production disappear from the account.\n\nOccurrences: the five preparation roles (#1); the provenance questions (#1, #5→0's circuit); the disappeared labour (#1, returned at #4).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
